       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 50 mg is five times the maximum recommended adult dose of 10 mg once daily. The usual range is 2.5 to 10 mg. A dose this high risks severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, peripheral edema, and prolonged toxicity, because amlodipine has a very long half-life. This looks like a possible typo, perhaps for 5 mg.\n\nCould you confirm which of these you want?\n- **5 mg** by mouth once daily, a common starting or maintenance dose.\n- **10 mg** by mouth once daily, the maximum dose.\n- **2.5 mg** by mouth once daily, which is typical for frail patients or those with hepatic impairment.\n- **50 mg** is truly intended. If so, please tell me the clinical rationale and I can enter it with a note. I'd also suggest pharmacy verification first.\n\nOnce you confirm, I'll enter the order right away."
      }
